    "aliases": [],
    "description": "Strict comparison is a comparison operator or a control structure that checks not only the value but also the type of the value. In other words, it does not apply any type-juggling to the values before processing. \n\nHere are the strict operators: ``==`` may be replaced with ``===``,  ``!=`` may be replaced with ``!==``, ``switch`` may be replaced with ``match``, ``in_array()`` with the third parameter ``strict`` set to true.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    //true\n    var_dump(1 == \"1\");\n    //false\n    var_dump(1 === \"1\");\n    \n    //true\n    var_dump(null == 0);\n    //false\n    var_dump(null === 0);\n\n?>",
